#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: measureless to man
#> pause: 40
#> must: # command:  sed -n -f
#> must: Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
#> not: pleasure dome
#> not: sunless sea
#> source: /an/p
# 2. The -n flag: copy nothing unless a p says so. McMahon 1.1: sed -n
# Here #ARGS passes -n to sed (see the command line in the output pane).
# Now only lines that reach a p function are written. The address /an/ is a
# context address: a pattern between slashes selects every line containing it.
# Lines 1, 3 and 4 contain "an"; the other two are never written at all.
# Try: remove the #ARGS line and save: those three lines now appear twice.
#ARGS -n
/an/p

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan
A stately pleasure dome decree:
Where Alph, the sacred river, ran
Through caverns measureless to man
Down to a sunless sea.
